From ab167b7a02646abf2e82cd3ac7cb66a556ddccdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:03:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] Training Genome: learn how THIS user grows best (the
 moat)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Beyond session-based DNA (which captures *preferences*), the Genome learns
*response patterns over months*: it segments history into ~monthly blocks,
computes per-block inputs (dominant rep range, weekly sets, frequency,
recovery gap) and the e1RM growth that block produced, then correlates
inputs -> growth to surface the user's personal growth drivers
(e.g. 'You grow best training 4-6 reps / 14 sets/week / 4x/week / 72h').

- domain/genome/TrainingGenome.kt: pure, offline, deterministic engine.
  Confidence scales with data (Emerging/Moderate/Strong by # of blocks);
  honest 'needs a few months' state when data is thin. No new table or
  migration — computed from existing sessions like the DNA engine.
- TrainingDnaViewModel: produces the genome from completed sessions.
- TrainingDnaInsightScreen: 'Your Training Genome' card near the top with
  per-dimension best values + confidence badge.

Verified: full domain compiles on kotlinc 1.9.22 (208 classes); 3 genome
logic tests pass in-sandbox (not-enough-data honesty, learns across 6
blocks -> STRONG + correct rep range, 4-block -> MODERATE). Rate metrics
normalised by active training span; single dominant rep-range reported.
No conflict markers. No tests committed.
